    {
      "task_id": "retrygate",
      "title": "Retry decision under coupled rules",
      "structure": "COUPLED_UNCERTAIN",
      "rationale": "Three small modules, one decision. Classification, attempt accounting and backoff are each trivial in isolation, and the failure modes live between them: whether a refusal consumes an attempt, whether a zero hint is a hint, whether the last slot may be spent on an unknown error. A worker given only one module cannot answer any of those questions, so the expected delegation benefit is low and the coordination cost is real.",
      "goal": "The retrygate project classifies errors and counts attempts, but retrygate/policy.py does not decide anything yet. Implement decide() so the documented retry rules hold, and verify with the public tests. Leave the classification and budget modules unchanged.",
