    {
      "task_id": "cascade",
      "title": "Power operator in a coupled lexer and parser",
      "structure": "COUPLED_UNCERTAIN",
      "rationale": "The lexer owns the operator set and the parser owns precedence and associativity. Neither file can be changed correctly without the other, and the sharp edges are exactly where they meet: a token the lexer emits but the parser associates wrongly, or a grammar rule the parser supports but the lexer never delivers. Delegating the two files to two workers splits one grammar and the integration cost is the work.",
      "goal": "The cascade project renders the parse tree of arithmetic expressions but only knows + - * / and unary minus. Extend it with the power operator ^, right-associative and binding tighter than multiplication, so the public tests pass. Keep the existing behaviour for every other operator unchanged.",
      "goal_digest": "sha256:25d55baa21ce8220eedcd492ace64e444beed87c96b8c95744efe0359190223b",
      "write_scope": [
        "cascade/lexer.py",
        "cascade/parser.py"
