  "stopping_rules": [
    "Every attempt enters the denominator; a failed or aborted run is never dropped or retried.",
    "A run that exhausts the budget is a result, not an incident: it is recorded, not repeated.",
    "The matrix is executed in the frozen order; an operator may stop the batch between cells for cost or infrastructure reasons, and a stopped batch is reported as incomplete together with the cells that ran.",
    "No cell is re-run because its outcome looks unhelpful. A re-run is a new, separately registered experiment.",
    "If the sandbox provider is unavailable, the affected cells are recorded as INFRASTRUCTURE_BLOCKED and the batch pauses; they are not silently skipped."
  ],
  "leak_rules": [
    "The oracle program and the reference implementation live on the Host and are never provisioned into an agent-readable workspace.",
    "The oracle runs after the agent stops, inside the sandbox, from a command the agent never sees.",
    "The goal text carries no statement about the experiment, no worker count and no delegation instruction.",
    "The private tool payload corpus is not published with the results.",
    "Raw evidence is collected before any summarising, so a reporting defect cannot lose a run."
  ],
